{"id":"n4-080","title":"～させてください","romaji":"〜sasete kudasai","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"Express a polite request to allow or permit someone to do something.","longExplanation":"The ～させてください grammar point is used to make a polite request to allow or permit someone to do something. It can be translated as 'please let me' or 'please allow me to' in English. It is formed by taking the causative form of a verb and adding ください.","formation":"Verb-causative form + ください","examples":[{"jp":"もう少し考えさせてください。","romaji":"Mou sukoshi kangaesasete kudasai.","en":"Please let me think a little more.","words":[{"surface":"もう少し","vocabId":"2005870","reading":"もうすこし"},{"surface":"考え","vocabId":"1281020","reading":"かんがえ","baseForm":"考える"},{"surface":"させ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"させる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"写真を撮らせてください。","romaji":"Shashin o torasete kudasai.","en":"Please let me take a photo.","words":[{"surface":"写真","vocabId":"1321900","reading":"しゃしん"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"撮ら","vocabId":"1298790","reading":"とら","baseForm":"撮る"},{"surface":"せ","vocabId":"2147990","reading":"せ","baseForm":"せる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"もうちょっと練習させてください。","romaji":"Mou chotto renshuu sasete kudasai.","en":"Please let me practice a little more.","words":[{"surface":"もう","vocabId":"2081490","reading":"もう"},{"surface":"ちょっと","vocabId":null},{"surface":"練習","vocabId":"1559160","reading":"れんしゅう"},{"surface":"さ","vocabId":"1291070","reading":"さ","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"せ","vocabId":"2147990","reading":"せ","baseForm":"せる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[6]},{"jp":"